= Project Integration Management 
== Project Integration Management

Project Integration Management is the process of identifying, defining, combining, and coordinating all project management activities within the project management process groups. It connects all project knowledge areas and processes and ensures that all parts of the project work together smoothly. Integration is required from the beginning to the end of the project, and the project manager plays a vital role in coordinating different activities throughout the project life cycle.

=== Need for Integration Management
+ *Manage Change and Communication:* Helps control changes and maintain effective communication among stakeholders.
+ *Reduce Time and Cost:* Proper coordination avoids delays and unnecessary expenses.
+ *Involve Stakeholders Early:* Ensures stakeholders provide support and feedback at the right time.
+ *Make Results Visible:* Helps track project progress and performance clearly.
+ *Identify Problems Early:* Helps find issues and solutions before they become major problems.
+ *Use Past Experience:* Uses previous knowledge and lessons learned to improve project performance.

