== Project Scope Management

Project Scope Management is the process of defining, controlling, and managing what is included in the project and what is excluded. It ensures that the project delivers exactly what is required within the defined boundaries and prevents *scope creep* (uncontrolled expansion of scope).

*Key Purposes:*
- Defines all the work needed to complete the project.
- Ensures that the project team and stakeholders understand inclusions and exclusions.
- Helps in controlling changes to the scope during the project.
- Ensures that only agreed work is done and unnecessary tasks are avoided.

